#!/usr/bin/python3
"""tind-ai-ask: the AI assistant's chat window (Super+K). Runs as the human.

  tind-ai-ask              open the window (a second start brings the open window to the front)
  tind-ai-ask --open last  open the most recent chat (used by the CI self-test)
  tind-ai-ask --check      print whether the services answer and which providers have a key (no window)
  tind-ai-ask --templates  list the task templates (the chips above the input box; no window)
  tind-ai-ask --prices     list every model's price and price band (no window)
  tind-ai-ask --export [--unredacted]
                           export the Tind report and the system log to the export folder, like the window's Export
                           (no window; used by the CI self-test)
  tind-ai-ask --open prices  open the window on the Prices page
  tind-ai-ask --migrate    move chats from the old JSON store into the chat archive (also done when the window opens)
  tind-ai-ask --document FILE.md [--format md|docx|pdf|odt]
                           save a Markdown file to the Documents folder the way the window's Save as does (no window;
                           Word, PDF and ODT need LibreOffice Writer)

How a message travels (see /usr/share/doc/tind-ai-users/README):
  1. You type (Direct). Attaching system data (system log, Tind report, Steam logs, files) makes it Checked: the exact
     text is shown before it is sent. This window reads your own files; the system log is added by the local service.
  2. The local service (tind-ai-local, no network) hides names, addresses, keys and other secrets with fixed rules and
     saves the briefing. "Unredacted" skips the rules for one message.
  3. The provider's remote service (tind-ai-remote@PROVIDER) sends that saved briefing and writes the answer to your
     outbox. Nothing in an answer runs by itself.
Everything the window keeps for you is in one folder, ~/TindAI unless you pick another (menu > TindAI folder):
  ChatArchive/<provider>/  every chat as a readable Markdown file, kept until you delete the chat; the sidebar reads
                           this folder. Names and addresses are put back in (the provider only ever saw placeholders),
                           so the archive is as private as the rest of your home.
  Documents/               documents you save from an answer, as Markdown, Word, PDF or ODT (LibreOffice Writer
                           makes the last three, on this computer).
  Export/                  Export (header menu, or the + menu) writes the Tind report, the system log and the Steam
                           and Proton logs here, for AI apps outside this window such as Claude Desktop. Those apps
                           run as you, outside the walls, so the fixed rules hide names, addresses and keys first
                           unless you tick Unredacted. Every export replaces the previous one.
Folders and files are readable by you only. A folder synced elsewhere (Nextcloud and the like) sends its files on.
"""
import glob
import html
import json
import os
import re
import secrets
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import threading
import time

sys.path.insert(0, '/usr/lib/tind-ai')
import tindai  # noqa: E402

